column2:
In the SERVICE (data layer), not the handler — it's a data rule, not presentation.
It's check-then-act, so the count and the write go in ONE transaction (else the count
goes stale before the update — same race shape as read-modify-write).
  const others = await tx.userRole.count({ where: { ...active, user: { id: { not: target } } } });
  if (others === 0) return "last_manager";
Keep the definition of "active" IDENTICAL across every query, or guard and counted set drift.
